{"slug":"star-pyramid","title":"Pyramid of Stars","topic":"basics","difficulty":"medium","order":55,"tags":["loops","nested-loops","patterns"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Counting spaces and stars per row","body":["A centred pyramid has two kinds of characters in each row: the spaces on the left and the stars. Work out how many of each row `i` (from 1 to `n`) needs. For `n = 4`:",{"code":"   *        row 1: 3 spaces, 1 star\n  ***       row 2: 2 spaces, 3 stars\n *****      row 3: 1 space,  5 stars\n*******     row 4: 0 spaces, 7 stars"},"The spaces are `n - i` and the stars are `2 * i - 1`. Inside each row you therefore need two inner loops one after the other: one for the spaces, one for the stars.","The judge compares your output word by word, so only the stars of each row matter to it. Still print the spaces: it keeps the picture right and trains the habit of getting the layout exactly as asked."]},"statement":["Given `n`, print a pyramid of stars with `n` rows. Row `i` (from 1) has `n - i` spaces followed by `2 * i - 1` stars."],"inputFormat":["A single integer `n`."],"outputFormat":["`n` rows forming a centred pyramid."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 50"],"examples":[{"input":"3\n","output":"  *\n ***\n*****\n","note":"Rows: 2 spaces + 1 star, 1 space + 3 stars, 0 spaces + 5 stars."}],"hints":["Row `i` has `n - i` leading spaces and `2 * i - 1` stars. Check this for `i = 1` and `i = n`.","In each row use one inner loop for the spaces and a second inner loop for the stars.","End each row with a line break."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["For each row the first inner loop prints `n - i` spaces and the second prints `2 * i - 1` stars. The widest row has `2n - 1` stars and no leading space."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(1).","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\n\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    for _ in range(n - i):\n        print(\" \", end=\"\")\n    for _ in range(2 * i - 1):\n        print(\"*\", end=\"\")\n    print()\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int k = 0; k < n - i; k++) {\n            cout << \" \";\n        }\n        for (int k = 0; k < 2 * i - 1; k++) {\n            cout << \"*\";\n        }\n        cout << endl;\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            for (int k = 0; k < n - i; k++) {\n                System.out.print(\" \");\n            }\n            for (int k = 0; k < 2 * i - 1; k++) {\n                System.out.print(\"*\");\n            }\n            System.out.println();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3\n","output":"  *\n ***\n*****\n"},{"input":"1\n","output":"*\n"},{"input":"2\n","output":" *\n***\n"},{"input":"4\n","output":"   *\n  ***\n *****\n*******\n"},{"input":"5\n","output":"    *\n   ***\n  *****\n *******\n*********\n"},{"input":"10\n","output":"         *\n        ***\n       *****\n      *******\n     *********\n    ***********\n   *************\n  ***************\n *****************\n*******************\n"},{"input":"50\n","output":"                                                 *\n                                                ***\n                                               *****\n                                            